// TIFF - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// TIFF: an image format with a real field for human-readable text.
// Tag 270, ImageDescription, type 2, ASCII, thirteen bytes plus
// the NUL that terminates an ASCII count.
//
// This is the one of these six whose greeting a reader will
// actually display: `Hello World!` in thirteen bytes, which is
// what `identify` prints and what a browser's image panel shows.
// Little endian, magic 42, one IFD entry, and the next-IFD
// pointer is zero because there is no second one.
//
// tiff: 39 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 49 49 2A 00 08 00 00 00 01 00 0E 01 02 00 0D 00 |II*.............|   <- 0000
// 00 00 1A 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 |..........Hello |   <- 0010
// 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 00                            |World!.|   <- 0020
